## Overview
Problem Description
Users cannot send emails using a shared mailbox identity even after permissions are assigned.

Symptoms:
“You do not have permission to send on behalf of this user”
Email sent from personal address instead of shared mailbox
Send As option missing in Outlook

## Common Cause
- Send As permission not fully propagated
- Outlook cache not updated
- Autodiscover not refreshed
- Shared mailbox not fully converted or configured

## Troubleshooting Steps
- Confirm Full Access exist
- Wait for Propagation Delay
- Can take 30 minutes to 2 hours

## Restart Outlook / Re-login
- Close Outlook completely
- Sign out of Office 365
- Sign back in

